# Public prose style (blog + build log)

Technical and crypto-native readers treat dense em-dash punctuation as an AI tell. Prefer a human operator voice.

## Dashes

- **Do not use em dashes (`—` / `&mdash;`) as clause separators.**
- Prefer periods, commas, colons, parentheses, or a short new sentence.
- For a same-month week range in build log HTML, use an unspaced en dash (`Week of July 21&ndash;27, 2026`). When the week crosses a month, match the runbook: `Week of September 30, 2026 &ndash; October 4, 2026`. In blog Markdown prefer a simple hyphen (`July 21-27`) unless matching an established HTML pattern.
- Do not stack multiple dash asides in one sentence.

### Avoid

```text
Messy was exposed — founders lost money — then the market recovered.
```

### Prefer

```text
Messy was exposed because we had capital on that venue. The market sold off hard, then clawed back.
```

## Voice

- Direct, concrete, evidence-led. Short and medium sentences.
- Avoid triad cadence and “What X / What Y / What Z” stacks unless a tight list truly helps.
- Avoid hedge filler (“we do not believe…”, “before anyone quote-tweets…”) when a factual claim works.
- Keep commitments checkable. Skip thin-market or LP microstructure asides unless the user explicitly asks for them.
- Franco/Messy voice: accountable without courtroom theater or victory-lap tone.
